---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Docs" description="Getting started, publishing, graphics and format guidance for PlayMAKER, with current product availability." path="/docs/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Guides & documentation</p><h1>Find your starting line.</h1><p class="section-lede">Start with a released tool, follow its user path and move to source setup only when you want to contribute.</p></div></section>
  <section class="page-section"><div class="shell copy-section">
    <div class="callout"><p><strong>Availability:</strong> <a class="inline-link" href="/products/webmaker/">WebMAKER Studio 0.2.0</a> is a stable Windows release. <a class="inline-link" href="/products/postmaker/">PostMAKER 0.3.0</a> is available as a PWA and unsigned Windows app. TagMAKER 0.1 remains a source alpha; VideoMAKER remains in early development.</p></div>
    <h2 id="start">Start a first club</h2>
    <ol><li><a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/webmaker/releases/download/v0.2.0/WebMAKER.Studio_0.2.0_x64-setup.exe">Download WebMAKER Studio 0.2.0</a>. The installer is unsigned.</li><li>Install Git for Windows with Git Credential Manager if you want Studio to create, clone or publish GitHub repositories.</li><li>Open Studio, select <strong>Create a new club</strong>, then choose the club identity, basketball or football, theme, first season and destination.</li><li>Optionally create a public GitHub repository through Studio. Wait for GitHub Actions to complete before treating the Pages site as live.</li><li>Continue with the illustrated <a class="inline-link" href="/products/webmaker/#user-guide">WebMAKER user guide</a>. Manual cloning belongs to the contributor path.</li></ol>
    <h2 id="studio">What Studio performs</h2><p>Studio creates a clean project from its bundled starter, initializes <code>main</code>, and can use Git Credential Manager to create a public repository, push it and enable the included Pages workflow. It can also clone a WebMAKER repository or open one already cloned locally. Existing destination folders are never overwritten. Organization policies may still require approval, and a successful push does not prove Pages deployment has finished.</p>
    <h2 id="graphics">Create match graphics</h2><p><a class="inline-link" href="https://playmaker-apps.github.io/postmaker/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open PostMAKER ↗</a> to create post, story and square graphics in the browser, or install the Windows 0.3.0 desktop application. Both use the same editor and project format. The PWA needs one successful online visit before offline use. Browser storage is not a permanent backup, so export JSON or ZIP files regularly. See the <a class="inline-link" href="/products/postmaker/#user-guide">PostMAKER user guide</a>.</p>
    <h2 id="pages">This organization website</h2><p>This PlayMAKER organization site is an Astro project and is separate from a WebMAKER club project. To run it locally:</p><pre><code>npm ci
npm run dev
npm test
npm run build</code></pre><p>A push to this repository's <code>main</code> branch builds and deploys the static site through GitHub Actions. Pull requests build without deploying.</p>
    <h2 id="formats">Formats & data exchange</h2><p>WebMAKER public club data can be imported by PostMAKER. TagMAKER uses compatible WebMAKER roster paths and can export per-game statistics plus versioned JSON. The <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/playmaker-schema" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">shared PlayMAKER schema repository ↗</a> contains cross-product contracts. VideoMAKER import is not implemented yet.</p>
    <h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Which products can I install today?</summary><p>WebMAKER Studio 0.2.0 and PostMAKER Desktop 0.3.0 have public Windows x64 installers. They are unsigned. PostMAKER also has a public PWA. TagMAKER has public alpha source but no Windows installer; VideoMAKER has no application release.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Do I need an account or AI?</summary><p>PostMAKER core editing needs no account or GitHub access. WebMAKER uses GitHub only for optional repository and Pages workflows. Core PlayMAKER workflows do not require an AI service.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Are all products fully integrated?</summary><p>No. Released connections are documented on the <a class="inline-link" href="/ecosystem/">ecosystem status page</a>. VideoMAKER integration remains planned.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Where should I report an issue?</summary><p>Use Issues in the relevant public repository when enabled, or start from the <a class="inline-link" href={site.orgUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PlayMAKER organization ↗</a>.</p></details>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
